+1.  **Initialization:** Initialize the octree update using down-sampled projections.
+2.  **Coarse Update Phase (Topology & Density):** During the down-sampled update step, optimize the densities of the density grid inside each node. Use low-resolution projections to reduce the impact of high noise during octree updating [S1].
+3.  **Structure Locking:** After several epochs, fix the structure of the octree.
+4.  **Fine Update Phase (Density Only):** Use the original projections to optimize only the density grid of each node [S1].
+5.  **Density Initialization:** Initialize the density grids for the final optimization step from their down-sampled version [S1].
+6.  **Loss Metric:** Use the standard deviation (SD) of each node as the octree-update loss metric [S1].
 
