 ## Background
-The coarse-to-fine octree update strategy was introduced in the context of cryo-electron tomography (cryo-ET) reconstruction and denoising [S1]. It addresses the challenge of high noise in cryo-ET projections, which can destabilize standard differentiable rendering updates. By using down-sampled projections for initial topology optimization, the method achieves more stable and accurate reconstructions [S1].
+The coarse-to-fine octree update strategy was introduced in the context of cryo-electron tomography (cryo-ET) reconstruction and denoising [S1]. It addresses the challenge of high noise in cryo-ET projections, which can destabilize standard differentiable rendering updates. By using down-sampled projections for initial topology optimization, the method accelerates updating and reduces noise impact [S1].
 
